## Run notes

- **blink resolvability** - Round 1's median sampling interval is ~334 ms, which is the mean spontaneous blink duration (334 ms, VanderWerf et al. 2003, J Neurophysiol 89(5):2784-96, doi:10.1152/jn.00557.2002 - spontaneous blink 334 +/- 67 ms). A blink therefore occupies 0-1 samples and blink RATE is not recoverable in Round 1 at any threshold; only extended closures are. Blink rate is reported for Round 2 (120 Hz) only.
- **IMU deferred** - R2-01 BOR: head motion deferred by author ruling 2026-07-31; not read in this pass
